            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0786" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.7111/288</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Charles W. Hill of the Executive Department of the
                        State of Rhode Island to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Providence</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-31">December 31, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received January 2,
                        1935.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Phillips</hi>: With reference to your
                    letter of October 23 at the request of Governor Green I am sending to you the
                    enclosed check for $26 to reimburse Albert A. Amiaud, chauffeur to the Rumanian
                    Minister in Washington, for fine and costs paid by him to the third District
                    Court of this state.</p>
                <p>Trusting this is a satisfactory adjustment of this matter I am,</p>
                <p>Yours very truly</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles W. Hill</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
